===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[withdrawal]], especially of [[armed forces]].
# The [[change]] of the [[flight]] of an [[aircraft]] from a [[dive]] to [[level]] or [[climb]]ing flight.
# An object, such as a [[newspaper]] [[supplement]], that can be [[pulled]] [[out]] from something else.
# {{lb|en|typography}} {{synonym of|en|liftout||quotation given special visual treatment}}
# An [[area]] by the side of a road where [[vehicle]]s may [[temporarily]] stop in safety. Typical pullouts allow [[driver]]s and [[passenger]]s to safely exit the vehicle but rarely have additional [[amenities]].
#: {{syn|en|turnout}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Paul Elias; Phoung Le|title=CHP: Deadly SUV Cliff Crash May Have Been Intentional|url=https://www.usnews.com/news/best-states/california/articles/2018-04-01/chp-deadly-suv-cliff-crash-may-have-been-intentional|accessdate=2018-04-05|work=www.usnews.com|publisher=Associated Press;U.S. News and World Report|date=2018-04-01|passage=Capt. Greg Baarts with the CHP Northern Division says information pulled from the SUV's software shows the vehicle was stopped at the highway '''pullout''' before it accelerated straight off the cliff.}}
# {{lb|en|surfing}} The ending of a [[period]] of surfing by navigating the [[surfboard]] into or over the back of a [[wave]].
#* {{quote-av|1=en|year=1966|director=Bruce Brown|title={{w|The Endless Summer}}|text=Here's a pretty strange '''pullout'''. An "El Rollo." When Corky does something strange, everyone for 50 yards knows all about it.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Matt Warshaw|title=The Encyclopedia of Surfing|page=482
|passage=Most '''pullouts''', then and today, are done by simply angling or pivoting the board up and over the wave crest.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=John Engle|title=Surfing in the Movies: A Critical History|page=131
|passage={{...}} Machado, who turns what might seem like a handicap, that lankiness, to rubbery advantage in his sinuous carving and slackly cool '''pullouts'''.}}
# The [[coitus interruptus]] method of [[birth control]].

